      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-139750",
      ":question/problem": "A biologist has recorded data on a pine tree's age (in years) and height (in feet). This data is shown below. \n\n| Age $(x)$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Height $(y)$ | $1.2$ | $2.5$ | $3.6$ | $4.5$ |\n\nFind the line of the form $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above. According to the model, what will be the tree's height after $8$ years, assuming the trend continues?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that*\n\n$$\n({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}15 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{X}^{T}y=[\\begin{aligned}11.8 \\\\ 35\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n*where $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector.*"
